SELF_HELP_STOP.detail:
Measured against LD-ME-03 and the contract exclusions. 'When to stop and get help' carries:
- the wrong branch (Class D/E/civil-type);
- a later adjudication or conviction;
- a pending proceeding;
- three years not run, or the discharge date unknown;
- firearm prohibitions ('firearm prohibitions are not removed by sealing.', verbatim in ME-maine.json);
- 'erases the record';
- immigration.
The packet does not send an automatic-branch participant to file. Track me-seal-gen's 'Never use 'expungement' in Maine participant copy' holds: the word does not occur in the instructions or either fixture. 'Maine seals; it does not expunge' is the track's own wording.
